Subject: [PATCH] controller: remove a wired neighbor only on its parent's report

handle_dead_neighbors() compares the 1905 neighbors in a Topology Response
with the neighbors the database holds for the reporter. A missing wireless
neighbor is removed only when its bSTA uses a BSS of the reporter. A missing
wired neighbor is removed whoever reports it missing.

A wireless Agent that leaves a wired Agent's backhaul BSS stops listing that
wired Agent as a neighbor once 63 s pass without its discovery messages. The
controller then removed the wired Agent, its radios and its stations from the
model, although it stayed connected to its own parent and kept sending
reports. Those reports only refresh Agents the database still knows ("Agent
with mac is not found in database"), so the Agent stayed missing until it
restarted. In the lab this happened in four of the six backhaul-wired-parent
runs that played on 30 Sep, on the first report after prpl-agent-03, back
from the wired prpl-agent-05, aged it out.

Remove a missing wired neighbor only when the reporter is the wired parent
that the Ethernet neighbor graph inferred for it. When that parent is not
known, keep the Agent; its parent's own report still removes it. Wireless
neighbors are unchanged. Upstream master (e90ebe9) has the same code.

tests/test_dead_neighbor_removal.py compiles the function before and after
the change. The unpatched function must remove the wired Agent when a
wireless neighbor roams off it; both must remove a wired child that its
parent no longer reports and keep the wireless rules.

--- a/controller/src/beerocks/master/tasks/topology_task.cpp
+++ b/controller/src/beerocks/master/tasks/topology_task.cpp
@@ -1027,58 +1027,66 @@ void topology_task::handle_bss_configuration_report_tlv(
 void topology_task::handle_dead_neighbors(const sMacAddr &src_mac, const sMacAddr &al_mac,
                                           std::unordered_set<sMacAddr> reported_neighbor_al_macs)
 {
     LOG(TRACE) << "Checking if one of " << src_mac << " neighbors is no longer connected";
 
     auto neighbor_al_macs_on_db = database.get_1905_1_neighbors(al_mac);
     LOG(DEBUG) << "Comparing reported neighbors to neighbors on the database, neighbors_on_db="
                << neighbor_al_macs_on_db.size();
 
     for (const auto &neighbor_al_mac_on_db : neighbor_al_macs_on_db) {
 
         LOG(DEBUG) << "Checks if al_mac " << al_mac << " neighbor " << neighbor_al_mac_on_db
                    << " is reported in this message";
 
         // If reported al_mac is on the db skip it, otherwise remove the node.
         if (reported_neighbor_al_macs.find(neighbor_al_mac_on_db) !=
             reported_neighbor_al_macs.end()) {
             continue;
         }
 
         std::shared_ptr<Agent> neighbor = database.get_agent(neighbor_al_mac_on_db);
         if (!neighbor) {
             LOG(ERROR) << "Failed to get neighbor instance";
             continue;
         }
         std::shared_ptr<Station> neighbor_bh_sta = database.get_station(neighbor->parent_mac);
         if (!neighbor_bh_sta) {
             LOG(ERROR) << "Failed to get neighbor station instance";
             continue;
         }
 
         if (neighbor_bh_sta->get_bss()) {
             std::shared_ptr<Agent> neighbor_parent_agent =
                 database.get_agent_by_radio_uid(neighbor_bh_sta->get_bss()->radio.radio_uid);
             if (!neighbor_parent_agent) {
                 LOG(ERROR) << "Failed to get neighbor parent agent instance";
                 continue;
             }
             // It is possible that re-routing took place, and the node is now a neighbour of some
             // other node. To filter such cases, compare the current al_mac of the neighbor to the
             // al_mac of the reporter. If they are not equal then it means than the neighbor is
             // currently under another node.
             if (neighbor_parent_agent->al_mac != src_mac) {
                 LOG(ERROR)
                     << "The neighbor's parent's al_mac is not equal to the reporter's al_mac";
                 continue;
             }
         } else {
+            // Only the Agent a wired neighbor hangs off may declare it gone. A reporter whose
+            // backhaul left that neighbor stops listing it while it stays connected elsewhere.
+            auto neighbor_wired_parent = neighbor->backhaul.parent_agent.lock();
+            if (!neighbor_wired_parent || neighbor_wired_parent->al_mac != src_mac) {
+                LOG(DEBUG) << "Wired neighbor " << neighbor_al_mac_on_db
+                           << " is not a child of the reporter " << src_mac << ", keeping it";
+                continue;
+            }
             LOG(INFO) << "Wired connection";
         }
 
         LOG(DEBUG) << "known neighbor al_mac  " << neighbor_al_mac_on_db
                    << " is not reported on 1905 Neighbor Device TLV, removing the al_mac node";
         son_actions::handle_dead_station(tlvf::mac_to_string(neighbor->parent_mac), true, database,
                                          tasks);
         database.remove_agent(neighbor->al_mac);
     }
 }
